<title>UK: UNITED NEWS UP, PANMURE REMAINS POSITIVE.</title>
<headline>UNITED NEWS UP, PANMURE REMAINS POSITIVE.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in media giant United News &amp; Media Plc rose on Tuesday, with sources saying Panmure Gordon was pushing the stock after a recent period of underperformance.</p>
<p>The shares were up 21-1/2p to 691p by 1350 GMT, after easing from a high of 694p.</p>
<p>Panmure Gordon has a share price target of 821p, market sources said.  </p>
<p>Since the beginning of May the stock has underperformed the rest of its sector by nine percent and has lagged the All-Share index by 19 percent.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4027</p>
